id: pm-noq46i
title: "GH-851: compare init discovery roots by filesystem identity"
description: Nightly macOS and the PR's Windows runner expose equivalent tracker roots through different lexical aliases (/var versus /private/var and long versus 8.3 paths). Assert canonical filesystem identity without weakening current-versus-ancestor provenance or user-facing recovery-path coverage.
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[4]: github,macos,nightly,path-canonicalization
created_at: "2026-08-01T07:55:14.379Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-10T12:02:35.397Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-01T07:59:05.253Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-01T07:59:05.253Z"
author: "harness:codex"
resolution: fixed
expected_result: Current and ancestor init discovery roots compare equal across filesystem aliases on macOS and Windows while preserving discovery provenance and suggested-path semantics.
actual_result: "macOS /var aliases and Windows long versus 8.3 path aliases represented the same tracker with different lexical strings, causing false assertion failures."
